\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Cultural Arts Commissioner Suzanne Karger announced that a map of the sculptural artworks in Manhattan Beach is now available to the community; the map includes a QR code that provides the history and details of each piece; and copies can be found at the Manhattan Beach Art Center and on the City\rquote s website under the Parks and Recreation Department, Cultural Arts section.\line\line Interim Community Development Director Michael Codron invited the community to a meeting to discuss potential interim uses of the site at 400 Manhattan Beach Boulevard, to be discussed at Project Pulse at the Manhattan Heights Park Community Center on May 21, 2025, at 6:00 PM.\line\line Waste Management (WM) Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell reminded the community that, in observance of Memorial Day on Monday, May 26, 2025, all waste collection services will be delayed by one day; and gave a shout-out in recognition of Public Works Week, expressing gratitude to the Public Works Department and Public Works Director Erick Lee for their continued support and strong partnership with Waste Management (WM).\line\line Library Manager Josh Murray invited the community to celebrate the 10th anniversary of the Manhattan Beach Library with a special performance by extraordinary juggler Michael Drainer on Tuesday, June 3, 2025, from 11:00 AM to 12:00 PM; and reminded the community that the library will be closed on Monday, May 26, 2025, in observance of Memorial Day.\line\line Leadership Manhattan Beach High School Seniors Isabel L., Bryce N., and Lucas S. provided an update on their ongoing work with DaVinci Rise, an organization dedicated to delivering quality education to underserved and underprivileged students. This year's project centered on developing a Makerspace Cart to offer students a creative and hands-on learning environment.\line\line Leadership Manhattan Beach Class of 2000 representative Liz Laffoon invited the community to a special event, the Millennium Time Capsule Retrieval Ceremony, taking place at Veterans Parkway, across from the Joslyn Community Center on June 28, 2025, at 2:00 PM.\line\line Police Chief Rachel Johnson invited the community to the Annual Mark Vasquez Memorial Event Blood Drive at the Joslyn Community Center on May 22, 2025, from 9:00 AM - 8:00 PM.\line\line\pard Mayor Howorth announced that she attended the Manhattan Beach Library Speaker Series event featuring Chef Roy Choi, noting it was a wonderful community gathering.\cf1\i0\f1\par
